      "schema_version": "aspr_gear",
      "text": "The paper presents PHOTON, an imaging-guided photocleavage and sequencing workflow for selected tissue and subcellular regions, with demonstrations in granulosa cells, nucleoli, mitochondria, and stress granules. The method’s main retained limitations are ROI aggregation without preserved within-sample spatial identity and dependence on reliable image segmentation; direct benchmarks of capture bias and against submicron array-based platforms remain limited."
    },
